{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "ASP.NET Components"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about .Net framework. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Represent the solution outline to the problem presented by the customer through making case of use diagrams, facing the problem to the customer following rules and protocols of the organization."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming tools, diagrams of cases, and data flow diagrams."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Tense and Sentences with \"Made of\" to Talk about Components of ASP.NET"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the simple present to express facts or general characteristics of people or objects. <br><br>  You use the structure <span class= \"strong\">be + made + of</span>    to describe the nature or the components of an object. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the simple present, it is important to consider the subject, the verb and the complement. See the following structure: <br> <div class=\"center_text\">Subject +  Verb + Complement </div><br><br> Example: <br> <span class= \"italic\"> The application <span class= \"strong\">is</span>  very useful. <br> The sites <span class= \"strong\">work</span>  perfectly. <br><br> </span>  You can use the structure <span class= \"strong\">be + made + of   </span>  to talk about the components of ASP.NET. Remember that you have to conjugate the verb Be according to the subject. <br><br> <span class= \"italic\"> <ul> <li>An ASP.NET web application <span class= \"strong\">is made of </span>  multiple pages. </li> <li>ASP-NET pages <span class= \"strong\">are made of</span>   hierarchal classes. </li> </ul> </span> You can use this structure in affirmative, negative and interrogative statements:<br><br> <span class= \"italic\"> <ul> <li>An ASP.NET web application <span class= \"strong\">is made of</span>   multiple pages. </li> <li>An ASP.NET web application <span class= \"strong\">isn't made of </span>  multiple pages. </ li ><li><span class= \"strong\">Is </span>   an ASP.NET web application <span class= \"strong\">made of </span>  multiple pages? </li> </ul>  </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tThis system is based on object-oriented programming, and it is made of pages."}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tThere are many pages in an ASP.NET web application, and these pages are made of an object-oriented hierarchy of classes. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tEach variable inherits features from another one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "\tCLR offers services such control management and security checking."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Overview on Windows CardSpace"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Common Language Runtime o CLR is an environment to execute programs developed in .NET framework."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class= \"strong\"> Windows CardSpace </span> allows using identification cards by means of XLM based protocols to have access to websites that accept this technology. When a website requests user information, <span class= \"strong\"> Windows CardSpace </span> sends an encrypted identification card, the website analyses the information, and once the data is confirmed, the user can login without using a password.<br><br>  To avoid security issues and protect user privacy, <span class= \"strong\"> Windows CardSpace </span> only sends personal information to authorized sites and keeps track of the websites where it sends identification cards. <br>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "object-oriented programming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a programming language model based on objects and data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ASP.NET makes part of the .NET framework; this system is based on object-oriented programming."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "object-oriented hierarchy of classes"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a classification of different objects depending on inheritance properties"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many pages in an ASP.NET web application are made of an object-oriented hierarchy of classes in which each variable inherits features from another one."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "IIS"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "internet information service; a group of web servers"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(acronym)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When a user wants to have access to a page, he sends a request to a server or IIS. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "runtime system"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a mechanism to process computer language to execute a program "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The server processes the information, turns it into HTML code and, then, the server assigns the rest of the processing stage to the ASP. NET runtime system. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "metadata "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " binary information related to a program "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It has components such as common language runtime or CLR, metadata and assemblies, Windows presentation foundation, Windows cardspace, among others."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "just-in-time compilation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a process to transform an intermediate representation of a code to a computer language at the same time of a program execution"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It analyses the code to execute programs and it usually uses just-in-time compilation. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about the components of Net. Framework 3.5 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose the one you think is the most important. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare an oral presentation for your classmates talking about the component you chose."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present it to your classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about the components of Net. Framework 3.5"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare an oral presentation about a component of Net. Framework 3.5"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present it to my classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le03ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>James</strong>: The ASP.NET is part of the .NET framework. This system is based on object-oriented programming and it is made of pages.<br/>\n<strong>Katy</strong>: Do you mean ASP.NET uses a component object model?<br/>\n<strong>James</strong>: That's right! There are many pages in an ASP.NET web application, and these pages are made of an object-oriented hierarchy of classes in which each variable inherits features from another one.<br/>\n<strong>Katy</strong>:  How does this component model work?<br/>\n<strong>James</strong>: When a user wants to have access to a page, he sends a request to a server or IIS; the server processes the information, turns it into HTML code and then, the server assigns the rest of the processing stage to the ASP. NET runtime system. <br/>\n<strong>Katy</strong>:  What does the runtime system do?<br/>\n<strong>James</strong>: The runtime system gets the .aspx page and changes it into a .NET framework class. This is the result of inheritance process."}, {"time": "59000", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Katy</strong>: How many versions of .Net framework exist?<br/>\n<strong>James</strong>: There are many. If I remember correctly, there are eight, but the one I know better is .Net Framework 3.5.<br/>\n<strong>Katy</strong>: What is it made of? I mean, what components does it have?<br/>\n<strong>James</strong>: Well, it has components such as common language runtime or CLR, metadata and assemblies, Windows presentation foundation, Windows CardSpace, among others."}, {"time": "85500", "image": "enpe8n2le03ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Well, CLR offers services such control management and security checking. It analyses the code to execute programs and it normally uses just-in-time compilation. Windows presentation foundation is a tool to develop better visual features in an interface; and it is made of Windows applications that allow using media, animations, and files. <br/>\n<strong>Katy</strong>: What about Windows CardSpace?<br/>\n<strong>James</strong>: It is a technology to do identity control when we share personal data or download files."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le03ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the components of the ASP.NET model."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list the components of .Net Framework."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can present some characteristics of components of .Net Framework."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What is ASP.NET?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is ASP.NET important for web developers?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "How do ASP.NET components work?"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " James is doing an oral presentation about .NET Framework in his computer programming class. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type